---
description: Evidence Vault project rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Project: "Evidence Vault" — students store awards and activities once with evidence, select entries, and export an evidence PDF plus copy-ready answers for scholarship applications.

Stack: current Next.js App Router, TypeScript (strict), Tailwind CSS, Supabase (Auth + Postgres + Storage), pdf-lib. Dev server port 3001. Session refresh lives in proxy.ts (Next.js 16 renamed middleware.ts).

Rules:
- Use the App Router only. No Pages Router.
- Never hardcode keys. Use NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. Never use or expose the service_role key. Never commit .env.local.
- Email and password auth only. Do not add Google or other OAuth providers.
- Profile fields (username, year of study, major, hobbies) are optional. Do not block the dashboard when a profile is empty.
- Keep it simple: no extra libraries unless asked. No OCR, no AI features, no payments, no email sending.
- Every user-facing action needs visible loading, success, and error states.
- Validate inputs (required fields, file type, file size) and show clear error messages.
- Use sample/fake data only. No real personal documents.
- All database changes belong in supabase/schema.sql and must be safe to re-run.
